  "solutions": {
    "python": "# Single Number\n# Idea: To find the single number in an array where all other numbers appear twice, we can use the XOR operation. XORing a number with itself results in 0, and XORing any number with 0 results in the number itself. Therefore, if\u2026\n# Line comments below keep the same logic as the NeetCode 150 repo solution.\n\nclass Solution:\n    def singleNumber(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        result = 0\n        for num in nums:\n            result ^= num\n        return result\n",
